[{"id":"VRCE-1-75-1","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":75,"verse":1,"english":"Hearing Jamadagni's, words, the son of Dasaratha, in consideration of the presence of his father, said these words in subdued tone,","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.868,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-76-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1075001","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0a25335d83c99341de02949a1664d042d17c704e6360e8d0dafb6e7e213a78a9","compact":"451b9010877aa7a74877917c1e1582e42162569626273978e04b9ca8cde7b6aa","nasal":"b22797234aa5ae26112d63b540bf39748d1e9734b4051f8a357b74393bf9dcf6"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-75-2","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":75,"verse":2,"english":"O Bhrgu's son, I have heard of the deeds you have performed, resolved on avenging your sire. O Brāhmaṇa, I acknowledge that.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.582,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-76-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1075002","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"811049f1186a70f87cce8ac14082217aced6899f56dd4696d317d81ea7ce12dd","compact":"6c42ce1b2b84ed4eca7c78f54142554d562c2984a40df981a24698707609494d","nasal":"99c840eebebaa17b0a43ee0b1afc1396a26a2e50672eb092245e48df62880804"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-75-3","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":75,"verse":3,"english":"But, O Bhargava, you insulted me abiding by the Kșatriya duties, as pusillaniinous or devoid of prowess. Do you to-day witness my energy and vigour.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.867,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-76-3"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1075003","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a4aea33706807230cd44bbac664e06b9624862879196260c77bc01ad0cb91479","compact":"5df01689e54b925761bf10306c193566cdb738aead114fd7c4c3ad346011b333","nasal":"5df01689e54b925761bf10306c193566cdb738aead114fd7c4c3ad346011b333"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-75-4","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":75,"verse":4,"english":"Saying this, the enraged Rāghava, endowed with fleet vigour, took up Bhrgu's noble bow, together with the shaft.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.794,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-76-4"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1075004","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"234116813f5b448fc1d1e4fb6157a93cce92ec1a8f8e92c95b02c11fbb0838c5","compact":"58f9f8f1458229a5fb4fc9aeeffe046f59fd6d06bc345ead4f82680e86a7cd19","nasal":"58f9f8f1458229a5fb4fc9aeeffe046f59fd6d06bc345ead4f82680e86a7cd19"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-75-5","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":75,"verse":5,"english":"And fixing the string upon it he set the arrow. And then Rāma enraged addressed Jamadagni's son, Rāma, saying,","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.932,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-76-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1075005","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"23dc8c6e1768900fb8146ebb412ac284f4144a9a4b9691cb87b44b2af421cf1d","compact":"18001439c475224bbc7b17c8c73b721a9a1cc48dc48d99f50509ed972eba787d","nasal":"18001439c475224bbc7b17c8c73b721a9a1cc48dc48d99f50509ed972eba787d"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-75-6","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":75,"verse":6,"english":"You are a Brāhmana and through Viśvāmitra, art worthy of my homage. Therefore it is, o Rāma, that I can not let go this life-destroying shaft.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.882,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-76-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1075006","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"9fa747ecd173b69923c0b4f54d23fb064900153fe6fbf5f8cd