Id":"bala","sarga":75,"verse":9,"english":"And with the object of beholding Rāma holding that foremost of weapons, there assembled in a body the celestials and the saints, with the great-father at their head.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.817,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-76-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1075009","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a5f0e210ad89948b29f9bef980dd8a27924deb90bf646a68edeab7e7e342a885","compact":"e1a5b8c38cdce59112f6f4716e3505025dee178d7fe0cfb67c83a6b7637dc130","nasal":"e1a5b8c38cdce59112f6f4716e3505025dee178d7fe0cfb67c83a6b7637dc130"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-75-10","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":75,"verse":10,"english":"The Gandharvas and the Apsara and the Siddhas and the Cāraņas and the Kinnaras and the Yakşas and the Rākşasas and the Nagas assembled to behold that mighty wonder.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.769,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-76-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1075010","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3b9be58879c7eafeaf2ed7c2a78c0b6e2bb7ab8b00d90e7afcdcfffd557c4080","compact":"a1d22cbe887ef74a00de815a6e647386e2af8f70e4c0e5064da20b4e01e77cd1","nasal":"a3bfe957a918752c22a4bf580d6ddffe2bb2fd6ad3a813e91138c86c8532e6ae"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-75-11","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":75,"verse":11,"english":"And on Bhārgava's energy having been observed by Rāma bearing that best of bows, Jamadagni's son became bereft of prowess, and Rāma (Parasurāma) kept steadily eyeing Răma.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.877,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-76-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1075011","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"21b53a3af70e6b6f8d078ddd7bfe3c1095fbbb5616c76bda23