"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"4000cc31d7ce6fca669af5940b6706e76ec87271c09c2b58c236fd81de01bf51","compact":"3676d9eddd7cadf573144306ef79b8ed3050ee162cfdb9f1dbdc28a5cc84ed5f","nasal":"3676d9eddd7cadf573144306ef79b8ed3050ee162cfdb9f1dbdc28a5cc84ed5f"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-75-15","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":75,"verse":15,"english":"Therefore, O hero, it behove you not to destroy my course, O descendant of Raghu. With the speed of the mind shall I now wend my way to the Mahendra, best of hills.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.714,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-76-14"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1075015","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"590542e948877d85d7418a6f093eae312587eb0d2f8f9d302294cd3a37f1cdcf","compact":"396b8ef48cae6f955884795028399b48efdfa3f344b7e233f6b6799d292d7eb0","nasal":"24203da0acb4789a2da4384c15abe8fb782c018ce969f240e3198f8dae55567a"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-75-16","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":75,"verse":16,"english":"O Rāma, the regions I have conquered by my asceticism do you destroy with that foremost of arrows: let there be no delay about it.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.873,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-76-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1075016","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"dd78594044f8abf419030c3b4a5e102c4fa7da6e688ae40342f9c318b9e019c4","compact":"f3fb789c95bf5dd60078cdfb26d9389280316798fe5a96b38b745ac0f09c7f10","nasal":"f3fb789c95bf5dd60078cdfb26d9389280316798fe5a96b38b745ac0f09c7f10"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-75-17","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":75,"verse":17,"english":"Even from your handing of this bow I know you to be the chief of the celestials even that eternal one, the slayer of Madhu. Hail to you,","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-76-16"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1075017","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a823973032cf64cda3667dfb0d5aaaede1109fd42e03284d4c9340ac0922a450","compact":"33321e4af215d3fc2cb9f320f332d9b209b08b14e6fc13a74732e63ac6f296a2","nasal":"d60fc5d454e109e8e27516abf081e4db5bb56b49f539b6c9a2871045904cfe75"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-75-18","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":75,"verse":18,"english":"O vanquisher of foes! And all these celestials assembled are beholding you of unparalleled deeds, and without an antagonist in fight.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-76-17"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1075018","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d5cc9bea22b3249b5c586eaf08d728905617e065cc2273ccbce8a5bb8fc368ca","compact":"4a684ba0c1754c422051fae67bac218e6fcc1f4460710813666ce49bfaa30821","nasal":"e3870eb2b06fb0e8ed4aa3b9acffa19e0f809bd17e0af51e359a69d6d01ce8a3"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-75-19","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":75,"verse":19,"english":"And, O Kākutstha, neither ought I to be ashamed (because of this discomfiture); I have been baffled by the lord himself of the three worlds.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.881,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-76-18"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1075019","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"9be58b164074d24633a2828d69895c6b08b93c987f0f508b8517a7cd0a98a218","compact":"b9b2957ed9f03ed6eb57f83d593a5347b529a80cff83d4580fb96d7d2c60939d","nasal":"b9b2957ed9f03ed6eb57f83d593a5347b529a80cff83d4580fb96d7d2c60939d"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-75-20","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":75,"verse":20,"english":"And it behove, O Rāma to disengage this peerless shaft (from the bow), O you of noble vows; and on your shooting the shaft. I shall repair to that fore most of mountains, the Mahendra.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.871,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-76-19"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1075020","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"de398aad6318604055df0275df4f14f35a037b2da72b487fa40052bdaa3f9dab","compact":"64e641b67f50404a28dd0366d7d01137a05f25d593b95643ac68f90d0709ba57","nasal":"fddaa9682fd4b77d387c4a9293fb9029a5cacef7ea65b51f92fe790ddc55bc09"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-75-21","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":75,"verse":21,"english":"When Jamadagni's son, Rāma, had said this, the puissant and graceful son of Daśaratha, had said this, the puissant and graceful son of Dasaratha shot that excellent arrow.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-76-20"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1075021","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"8137f24b8e65752cc55ad1e6b7f50b86ab0eae1743c6b31abd6eae030d1fb457","compact":"360a16ad63cf54ca138cf4e93250b1927233b0715db54ebe2755a9bca93f4519","nasal":"360a16ad63cf54ca138cf4e93250b1927233b0715db54ebe2755a9bca93f4519"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-75-22","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":75,"verse":22,"english":"Then all the quarters became cleared of gloom; and the celestials and saints fell to extol Rāma when he had shot the arrow.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.864,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-76-22"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1075022","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"acc99305997e5f78532ce9432709cffa2879a6359e299331058a7fbebb421139","compact":"f505153f641c45e33d14d0537458ca85258ad5090d0446305f169d5049a26c04","nasal":"f505153f641c45e33d14d0537458